  "scope": "Iterates current-factor maximal packing (packedSchedule, wilsonSchedule) across arbitrary finite depths and proves active coordinate exhaustion by depth B.card, with an extensive initial Wilson block of size at least edgeCount n / 25. Proves that when active coordinates are exhausted, the evolved observable is constant and the unintegrated final covariance vanishes identically, reducing retainedCovariance and coarseCovariance to the pure finite sum exhaustedCoarseSum of coarse stage noise kernels. Realizes the two-staple aligned Gaussian approximation on the actual 4D periodic Wilson lattice (n > 1), proving exact cancellation of reference action terms in the 4-point mixed interaction rectangle and O(1/beta) convergence to -x*y/3 in beta^(-1/2) fluctuation coordinates. Formalizes the rank-one PSD finite-range continuum counterexample boxKernel and proves that its degree-4 contact-repaired pairing diverges as a -> 0+ on tests with nonzero box average, demonstrating that inter-scale cancellation or decay is necessary for continuum convergence of coarse kernels.",
  "results": {
    "covariance_exhaustion": {
      "empty_support": "When active B T N = empty and initial source support is contained in B, the evolved observable at depth N depends on the empty coordinate set and is literally constant.",
      "zero_final_covariance": "At any exhaustion depth N with active B T N = empty, covarianceAt mu T A0 F G N = 0 identically.",
      "pure_stage_sum": "Initial covariance equals the pure finite sum sum_{k < N} removedStageCovariance mu T A0 F G k with zero unintegrated remainder."
    },
    "iterated_maximal_packing": {
      "schedule": "packedSchedule D B selects chosenBlock at each stage from the true evolved support family supports D T k and active set active B T k.",
      "admissibility_and_disjointness": "packedSchedule_admissible proves factor-star independence at every depth; packedSchedule_disjoint proves pairwise disjointness of all stage blocks.",
      "strict_progress_and_exhaustion": "Whenever active B (packedSchedule D B) k is nonempty, packedSchedule D B k is nonempty and active cardinality strictly decreases; hence active B (packedSchedule D B) N = empty for all N >= B.card."
    },
    "wilson_extensive_schedule": {
      "definition": "wilsonSchedule n := packedSchedule (plaquetteEdges n) Finset.univ on the 4D periodic lattice of period n.",
      "extensive_first_block": "edgeCount n <= 25 * (wilsonSchedule n 0).card, so the first admissible independent block eliminates at least 1/25 of all lattice links.",
      "exhausted_coarse_sum": "At depth edgeCount n, retainedCovariance vanishes identically; retainedCovariance at depth J and coarseCovariance(J, edgeCount n - J) both equal the pure finite sum exhaustedCoarseSum of coarse stage noise kernels from J to edgeCount n - 1.",
      "repair_equivalence": "On the growing UV repair path, convergence of the degree-4 contact-repaired full Wilson covariance is equivalent to convergence of exhaustedCoarseSum."
    },
    "full_lattice_aligned_realization": {
      "configuration": "alignedConfig n x t s on the 4D periodic lattice (n > 1) sets selectedLink n x 1 to rotorUnit t, selectedLink n x 2 to rotorUnit s, and all other links to 1.",
      "staple_identity": "stapleSum n (alignedConfig n x t s) x 0 = alignedSum t s and exteriorStaple n x 0 (alignedExterior n x t s) = alignedSum t s.",
      "exact_rectangle_cancellation": "In the 4-point mixed interaction rectangle generatedMixedInteraction of the literal generated factor nextFactor (.inr (selectedLink n x 0)), the single-variable reference action terms cancel identically: generatedMixedInteraction_eq_starMixed.",
      "fluctuation_scaling_limit": "For beta >= max(1, R^2) and |x|, |y| <= R, |generatedMixedInteraction n z beta (x/sqrt(beta)) (y/sqrt(beta)) - (-x*y/3)| <= (3*R^4/2 + 9*R^2/10)/beta, converging to -x*y/3 as beta -> infinity."
    },
    "macroscopic_contact_obstruction": {
      "kernel": "boxKernel a R (x, y) = a^(-8) * boxIndicator R x * boxIndicator R y on the closed ball of radius R in R^4.",
      "properties": "Measurable, symmetric, nonnegative, bounded by 1/a^8, supported in |x - y| <= 2R, and positive semidefinite on all complex Schwartz test functions.",
      "divergence": "On any diagonal-disjoint real Schwartz product tensor f tensor g with positive ball integrals, the degree-4 contact-repaired pairing equals a^(-8) * boxFunctional R f * boxFunctional R g and diverges to +infinity as a -> 0+."
    }
  },
  "remaining": [
    "Prove uniform physical-scale bounds for the exhausted coarse covariance sum exhaustedCoarseSum and exhibit a nonzero separated reflected signal. Eliminating the unintegrated final covariance by exhaustion does not by itself bound the intermediate coarse stage noise kernels.",
    "Extend the full-lattice aligned two-staple Gaussian approximation (-x*y/3 mixed interaction limit) to general non-aligned backgrounds, large-field probabilities, and multi-step renormalization group flow.",
    "Supply quantitative inter-scale decay or cancellation across coarse stages. The formalized rank-one PSD finite-range counterexample boxKernel proves that measurability, symmetry, positive semidefiniteness, a^(-8) amplitude bounds, and macroscopic finite range alone do not imply continuum convergence after degree-4 contact subtraction.",
    "Prove compatible all-order renormalized correlation bounds, including higher partial-diagonal counterterms and mixed retained/noise cumulants.",
    "Prove the physical logarithmic bracket signs, physical coupling trajectory and nonzero normalization; then establish continuum reconstruction, symmetry and reflection positivity, relative transfer-energy gap, domains/cyclicity/spectrum and every compact simple gauge group. All twelve full Clay requirements remain open."
  ],
